From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: use librt's __cxa_thread_atexit_impl on powerpc64-ps3-elf

libsupc++'s __cxa_thread_atexit (thread_local objects with non-trivial
destructors) uses the C library's __cxa_thread_atexit_impl when
configure finds one, and otherwise registers the destructors through a
pthread key.  A key-based list runs in the key-destructor phase, in an
order relative to libstdc++'s own at-thread-exit key
(notify_all_at_thread_exit, promise::set_value_at_thread_exit) that
depends on registration order, while the standard requires a thread's
thread_locals to be destroyed before those notify.  librt provides
__cxa_thread_atexit_impl with a phase of its own that runs before the
key destructors; the check for it only runs for native builds, so define
HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL for the target, beside HAVE_TLS.

diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/configure b/libstdc++-v3/configure
index 2278c13..0f9ccd6 100755
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ -27538,6 +27538,11 @@ else
       powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
         $as_echo "#define HAVE_TLS 1" >>confdefs.h
 
+        # librt provides __cxa_thread_atexit_impl (its thread-exit cleanup
+        # runs thread_local destructors before the pthread key destructors);
+        # the check for it never runs in this branch.
+        $as_echo "#define HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL 1" >>confdefs.h
+
         ;;
     esac
     $as_echo "#define HAVE_HYPOT 1" >>confdefs.h
diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac b/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
index 1cb03be..b90ad4f 100644
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
@@ -346,6 +346,10 @@ else
     case "${host}" in
       powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
         AC_DEFINE(HAVE_TLS)
+        # librt provides __cxa_thread_atexit_impl (its thread-exit cleanup
+        # runs thread_local destructors before the pthread key destructors);
+        # the check for it never runs in this branch.
+        AC_DEFINE(HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT_IMPL)
         ;;
     esac
     AC_DEFINE(HAVE_HYPOT)
